# How many people left extreme poverty every day since 1990?
subtitle: "Guess how many people left extreme poverty on an average day since 1990, then see the headline no paper ran, and why it may soon stop."
tags: ["economics","data","history"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"The headline nobody printed\" note \"Every day for 35 years\""

## How many people left extreme poverty every day since 1990?
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - '1990'
      - '2025'
      - 2030?
    values:
      - 2300
      - 820
      - 780
    value_labels: true
    bar_colors: same
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 2600
    y_label: Millions in extreme poverty
    label_size: 30
sources:
    - id: roser
      title: The end of progress against extreme poverty?
      authors: Max Roser (Our World in Data)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/end-progress-extreme-poverty
      finding: on an average day in the last 35 years about 115,000 people left extreme poverty; 2.3 billion lived in extreme poverty in 1990, 817 million in 2025, a projected 782 million in 2030, rising after 2030; poverty line $3 a day
    - id: pip
      title: Poverty and Inequality Platform
      authors: World Bank
      year: 2025
      finding: the data behind Our World in Data's extreme poverty estimates, at the $3-a-day international poverty line

    icon paper size 320 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of newspaper hidden true
    box hq "? out of poverty today" #2f2b26 x 500 y 400 width 600 height 90 font_size 44 style.fill #fffdf6 hidden true
    box head "115,000 out of poverty today" #2f6b8f cites ["roser"] x 500 y 400 width 640 height 90 font_size 44 style.fill #fffdf6 hidden true
    icon stadium size 380 set twemoji x 380 y 450 icon_look picture of stadium hidden true
    text stad_l "≈ 1 stadium" #2f6b8f x 760 y 450 font_size 46 hidden true
    text slow "slowing" #b5482e cites ["roser"] x 760 y 500 font_size 52 hidden true
    text rise "after 2030: rising" #b5482e cites ["roser"] x 760 y 420 font_size 44 hidden true
    icon paper2 size 200 set twemoji x 770 y 560 icon_look picture of newspaper hidden true
    text end_q "tomorrow's headline?" #b5482e x 770 y 420 font_size 40 hidden true

    card title "How many left poverty each day?"

A: Here is a headline no newspaper ever ran. Since 1990, on an average day, how many people left extreme poverty?
    draw paper

B: In one day? A few hundred, tops. Poverty doesn't move that fast.
    draw hq

    erase paper hq

    ask "Set the counter: people leaving extreme poverty on an average day." estimate.min 10 estimate.max 1000000 estimate.value 115000 estimate.unit "a day" estimate.log true store g default "500" relative true tolerance 0.3
        right: Close: you said {g}, and it is about {g.true} people a day.
        wrong: You said {g}. It is about {g.true} people, every single day.

    erase estimate_1

A: A hundred and fifteen thousand. Every day, for thirty-five years.
    draw paper head

    erase paper head

B: Wait, every day? That's a packed football stadium, walking out of poverty daily!
    draw stadium stad_l

    erase stadium stad_l

A: Yes. In 1990, about two point three billion people lived on less than three dollars a day.
    draw axes bar_1

A: By 2025, about eight hundred million, even though the world added billions of people.
    draw bar_2

B: So why did no paper ever print it?
    highlight bar_1 bar_2

A: Because it happens slowly. One good day looks like nothing, while bad news arrives all at once.
    text slownews "good news is slow" #2f6b8f x 760 y 480 font_size 46

    erase slownews

A: And here is the catch: the fall is slowing. The forecast for 2030 is still about seven hundred and eighty million.
    draw bar_3 slow

A: Most of the poorest now live in economies that barely grow, so after 2030 the number is expected to rise again.
    draw rise

    erase slow rise

B: So the best headline of our lifetime might stop running.
    draw paper2 end_q

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    shape pg #2f2b26 shape rect x 470 y 470 width 760 height 420 style.fill #fffdf6 hidden true
    text mast "THE DAILY" #2f2b26 x 470 y 620 font_size 70 hidden true
    path rule #2f2b26 points [[120,575],[820,575]] style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    text h "? escape" #b5482e x 470 y 480 font_size 120 hidden true
    text h2 "poverty today" #2f2b26 x 470 y 350 font_size 90 hidden true
    thumb band "The headline nobody printed" kind band hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon sun size 260 set twemoji x 220 y 460 icon_look picture of sunrise hidden true
    text n "? a day" #2f6b8f x 640 y 510 font_size 170 hidden true
    text y "for 35 years" #2f2b26 x 640 y 330 font_size 80 hidden true
    thumb band "Out of extreme poverty" kind band hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon p1 size 200 set twemoji x 150 y 450 icon_look picture of "person walking" hidden true
    icon p2 size 200 set twemoji x 330 y 450 icon_look picture of "person walking" hidden true
    icon p3 size 200 set twemoji x 510 y 450 icon_look picture of "person walking" hidden true
    text x "× ?" #b5482e x 760 y 450 font_size 160 hidden true
    thumb band "Since yesterday. Again." kind band hidden true
